<article class="env-lemma" id="05UT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05UT">Lemma <span data-tag="05UT">10.39.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $\{ M_ i, \varphi _{ii'}\} $ be a directed system of flat $R$-modules. Then $\mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _ i M_ i$ is a flat $R$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows as $\otimes $ commutes with colimits and because directed colimits are exact, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00DB" data-tag="00DB">10.8.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>